 "notes": "The reef off the point of Ras Abu Soma: the wall on the north side where the shelf narrows, the sandy slope with coral blocks and the plateau at about 25 m with big table corals to the south, the drop-off beyond it at 25-30 m, the moorings at the corner by the sandy lagoon, and the usual drift south with the current. The zones come from dive-centre descriptions (4eversea), so extents are approximate. The origin is set on the dive site (26.8451, 34.0038); the site's stored coordinates lie about 1.4 km inland.",
